## Protected Files

- **File access override:** read any path the user provides, regardless of `.gitignore`.
- **Do NOT modify unless explicitly asked:**
  - `package.json`, `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml` (dependencies, engines)
  - `docker-compose*.yml`, `Dockerfile.*`
  - `.env*` (except `.env.example`)
  - Framework `curricula/**`, `standards/**`, `references/**`, and `drills/**` for learner-specific content (copy into `.training.mlt/programs/` instead)
  - `.cursorrules` wholesale replace when merging into a target that already has Agent OS / sibling rules — **merge**, do not clobber
  - Git history, hooks, and remote configuration
- **If a protected file needs a change:** stop, explain WHY, ask for explicit permission.

---

## Data Privacy & Security

- **Sensitive learner / company data:** keep production, customer, and confidential company details out of committed docs unless the user explicitly directs inclusion; prefer redacted scenarios in drills.
- **No PII in logs/artifacts:** never log full objects with PII (emails, phones, gov IDs, salaries) — use roles/internal labels; sanitize errors.
- **Secret scrubbing:** before reading/emitting text, ensure no keys/tokens/passwords appear (`[REDACTED]`); never display credentials or raw `.env`; never commit API keys or secrets to any file.
- **Test / drill data:** synthetic/mock only; do not hardcode real emails/IDs from the learner's org without permission.
- **File hygiene:** delete temp files after use; write exports/scratch to `tmp/` / `.tmp/`, not the framework or source tree.
- **Model safety:** never download or execute untrusted model weights. Only use models from verified sources (Hugging Face verified publishers, official repos). Warn the learner before downloading any model >1GB.
- **API key protection:** never hardcode API keys in tutorials or labs. Use environment variables or `.env.example` patterns.

---

## Workflow Rules (anti-destructive)

### Planning
- Programs and session plans live under `.training.mlt/`.
- Wait for approval before large custom programs when the user asked for analysis only (unless `-y`).
- Confirm before editing when scope is unclear.

### Deletion
- **NEVER delete files** without explicit user permission in the same message.
- Never `rm -rf` project trees, wipe `.training.mlt/`, or truncate learner history "to clean up."
- Temp cleanup is limited to files **this session created** under `tmp/` / `.tmp/` — still prefer asking if unsure.

### Overwrite & merge
- Prefer **no-overwrite** / append / merge. Never wholesale-replace `.cursorrules`, active programs, or HANDOFF without explicit request.
- Deploy `update` lists merge candidates; agent merges rules-aware — does not blind-replace.

### Git
- NEVER `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly requests it in the same message.
- Never modify history (**rebase, amend of others' commits, force-push**) without explicit request.
- Never update git config.
- When the user requests commit: stage safe paths, commit, show `git log -1 --oneline` + `git status -sb`; no "committed" claim without a SHA.
- Provide commit commands for the user when they will commit themselves.

### No attribution / no signatures
- Never add "Generated by", "Created by", dates-as-signatures, or agent signatures to files.
- **No `Co-authored-by:` trailers (mandatory)** — never add co-author trailers (Cursor/Copilot/any agent) or `--trailer`.

### Target-repo coexistence
- When scaffolding into a repo that already has Agent OS / app code: do not rewrite app source, dependencies, or CI unless asked.

---

## Verification & Communication

- **Before "complete":** confirm artifacts exist under `.training.mlt/` (or framework paths if the task was framework work); report actual paths/output, not assumed success.
- **On failure:** report exact error, diagnose, fix if in scope, re-run checks.
- **Scope:** declare scope first; only deliver what the question asked.
- **Communication:** be concise; surface blockers early; label uncertainty; distinguish confirmed facts / inferences / proposals.

---

## Commit Message Format

- Plain text; no surrounding quotes or wrapping parentheses.
- Subject (<=72 chars, imperative): `type: description` (or `REF-123: subject` when a ref is known).
- Optional body after a blank line: explain **why**, not the file list.
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`, `test`.

---

## Documentation layout (framework vs learner memory)

| Path | Layer |
|------|-------|
| `skills/`, `curricula/`, `standards/`, `references/`, `drills/`, `templates/`, `scripts/` | Framework (shared) |
| `.training.mlt/` | **All learner-specific memory** — profile, programs, sessions, labs, sources, assessments, progress |
| `.cursorrules` | Agent contract (local) |
| `.quick/` | Operator cheat sheets |

Hard rule: learner artifacts never live under the framework tree.
